\begin{exercise}
\label{exer:A.62}
\dcref{chA:A.62}
Suppose $\pi: \tilde{M} \to M$ is a covering map. Show that $\tilde{M}$ is compact if and only if $M$ is compact and $\pi$ is a finite-sheeted covering.
\end{exercise}


We will revisit smooth covering maps at the end of Appendix C.

